  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Your interdimensional charge leaves your foes off-balance and vulnerable.</p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisite:</strong> Dimensional Assault<sup>UC</sup></p>\n<p><strong>Benefit:</strong> When attacking with the special charge allowed by Dimensional Assault, your opponent is considered flat-footed. Your add one-half your mythic tier (minimum 1) to your bonus on attack rolls for charging, and if your charge attack hits you can make a combat maneuver check to reposition the target as a free action. This maneuver does not provoke attacks of opportunity. If you successfully reposition a non-mythic creature, you can expend one use of mythic power to make that creature flat-footed until the beginning of your next turn.</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/mythic-general-a-f-feats#toc90\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
